A||N||11||Rumor||Spoila paranoia||||1||
Z||000000||Rumor||11-28-2001||10:46 AM||||Have a lot of people had their spoilers ripped off? I will be installing one this weekend. Does anyone know of a way to lessen the chance that someone could just pull it off the back of the car (other then having me squat up in a tree with a sniper rifle)?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula88||11-28-2001||11:08 AM||||You mean the GT style rear decklid wing?  About all you can do it put some large fender washers on the underside of the decklid when you bolt it down.  That'll make it hard to just grab and rip the bolts up through the decklid.  But if it does get stolen that way, you'll have a lot more damage - and even if they don't get it off the car, they'll likely damage the wing anyway.<P>Try a car cover with an alarm?  Locked garage?  Armed security?||||reg||1
Z||000002||StuGood||11-28-2001||12:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Rumor:<BR><B>Have a lot of people had their spoilers ripped off?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>I think the answer is yes, it has happened to quite a few people.  A lady I once knew (1987 or thereabouts) had one (literally) ripped off her Fiero GT in her driveway - and she didn't live in a "bad" neighborhood, either.  Also, my GT had "spoiler wounds" in the rear decklid when I bought it.  So, it definitely happens.<P>For now, I just patched the wounds in my decklid.  If I decide to put a spoiler on, I think I will install a couple rectangular backup plates underneath the decklid's upper skin.  Each plate would be of .090"-thick 7075 aluminum (one per spoiler stanchion).  The plates would have two holes per (to pick up the 2 fasteners on each stanchion), and they would be as big as I could manage to sneak through the access holes in the bottom skin of the lid.<P>Wouldn't make it impossible to tear the spoiler off, but it would certainly be enough to deter the casual thief, I suspect.     ||||reg||3
Z||000003||camon||11-28-2001||01:16 PM||||I would try to use a metal plate (doesn't need to be real thick just solid....about the thickness of a penny).<BR>Cut it so it is long enough to go from one side of spoiler mounting hole to the other and drill holes in it to match the holes in the engine compartment lid then put your spoiler on bolting it through the metal plate (which is on the underside of engine compartment lid)!<BR>I would also paint it black so it would look better. <P>No thief could rip this off!<P>just my .02<P>------------------<BR>Keith<p>[This message has been edited by camon (edited 11-28-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000004||WampusCat||11-28-2001||02:19 PM||||1. Get several pounds of C4 plastic explosive.<BR>2. Mold it to the shape of your spoiler and cover with fiberglass.<BR>3. Oh...nevermind.||||reg||1
Z||000005||rockcrawl||11-28-2001||03:39 PM||||I had one stolen from my car while it was parked in a friend's driveway at night. It was an aftermarket replica, not an original. They pulled the bolts right through the decklid leaving some nasty splintery holes. This was shortly after the car was painted. I was pissed. <BR> A metal plate under the bolt heads will not save your wing. It will prevent the thief from using it because the stanchions will just break off and stay on the decklid. At this point he will be pissed and probably break your window just because he can't have your wing in one piece.<BR> I've seen Fiero wings on all sorts of cars. I've seen them on pickups, an old Supra, and just last week saw one on a Mustang.||||reg||1
Z||000006||artherd||11-28-2001||04:26 PM||||put a GPS tracker, an old old laptop, and an old cell phone glassed into the wing.<P>When somebody nabs it, just check your email, lookup the cordinants of their house, and BURN THE PLACE DOWN!<P>Then call the cops.  Maybe.<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000007||PAUL88GT||11-28-2001||06:27 PM||||The spoiler on the 86SE I am restoring had been torn off.  I had to buy a decklid and spoiler for $150 (a fair price for both).  I plan to use large washers under the decklid to make it harder to rip off after my paint job is completed.  My guess is it was more of a problem when the Fieros were new.  Now I think there are more desirable spoilers out there now attracting the attention of thieves.||||reg||1
Z||000008||DKOV||11-28-2001||06:34 PM||||Yeah... I suffer a bit from Spolia Paranoia both for the Fiero and my Lotus Esprit Turbo.  But also from Wheelia Paranoia.  I need to get locking wheel nuts on there FAST!<P>I like the idea of a troop of starving paratrooper pitbulls swooping in on wing snatching rice-boys  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>DKOV -<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Pyric||11-28-2001||06:42 PM||||Well, what ever you do DON'T buy a new one from the dealer.  The Suggested retail for the spoiler on my 85 GT was $1200.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>When I saw that I thought "damn, that's just about the blue book value.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>If you're really vengeful, every time you see one on another car you can rip it off and leave it on the ground.  You're bound to get them eventually. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Or you could just carve you're License # in the bottom and check everyone you come across when it disappears.<p>[This message has been edited by Pyric (edited 11-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||artherd||11-28-2001||10:23 PM||||I don't have locking nuts exactly, but I do have two different kinds of 'keyed' 'tuner style' lug nuts on Trav's 17s.<P>One is allen head style, the other *looks* like a wheel locking lug-nut, but it's actually a quasi-standard type of <P>Both require a black impact-wrench-steel key that goes between the gun and the nuts to remove.<P>I figure, if the thieves are smart enough, and want my wheels bad enough, to come prepared with two sets of keys, and the ability to pull the nuts I torque on with a 600lb-ft air gun, all withought waking the Trained Rabbid Crazy Under-fed abused Wolf that I keep in the passenger seat then they can have them  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Gotta figure something to do with the Porsche wheels (they use wheel bolts, no nuts/studs) there's probally a 'standard' wheel lock set I can get for a 996 I would imagine...<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DKOV:<BR><B> But also from Wheelia Paranoia.  I need to get locking wheel nuts on there FAST!<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000011||Rumor||11-28-2001||10:32 PM||||I LIKE the way you guys think!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I just bought a GT wing off ebay for 100 bucks, and the spoiler gaskets from the firo store for ten bucks. Take care.||||reg||1
